1
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:53,345
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS,
INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

2
00:00:53,471 --> 00:00:54,305
ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:55,264
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

4
00:00:55,431 --> 00:00:56,265
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED
SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

5
00:01:01,604 --> 00:01:02,980
What an attention seeker.

6
00:01:03,105 --> 00:01:04,857
You'd think she's quitting film.

7
00:01:04,982 --> 00:01:06,358
That makes no sense.

8
00:01:06,484 --> 00:01:08,652
If Lee Mi-do actually quits film,

9
00:01:08,778 --> 00:01:10,863
I'll send her my entire life savings.

10
00:01:10,988 --> 00:01:14,825
Muyeong Bank, 073-0214-5102-45.

11
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:16,952
It's peanuts, but I'll take it.

12
00:01:17,077 --> 00:01:19,497
What do you mean, peanuts? Hey!

13
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:24,043
Oh, Mom.

14
00:01:32,676 --> 00:01:34,678
The rice store owner's youngest son

15
00:01:34,804 --> 00:01:37,306
just passed the civil service exam.

16
00:01:37,431 --> 00:01:41,143
And the piano academy owner's
eldest daughter

17
00:01:41,268 --> 00:01:43,562
got into college on her fourth try.

18
00:01:43,687 --> 00:01:45,731
I really am quitting film.

19
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:53,447
Don't mind what Yeong-do says.

20
00:01:54,031 --> 00:01:57,910
Your fortune says you're a late bloomer.

21
00:01:58,035 --> 00:01:58,953
Your birth chart

22
00:01:59,745 --> 00:02:02,248
says good things take time for you.

23
00:02:02,373 --> 00:02:04,041
I said I'm really quitting.

24
00:02:05,668 --> 00:02:09,255
It's my turn to get the payout
from the merchants' savings club.

25
00:02:10,005 --> 00:02:12,299
I'll lend you that money, so don't worry.

26
00:02:12,424 --> 00:02:13,467
AFTER SPRING COMES WINTER

27
00:02:13,592 --> 00:02:16,095
Just focus on writing your script
for about two years.

28
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:19,598
I'll lend it to you without any interest--

29
00:02:26,021 --> 00:02:26,981
Hey!

30
00:02:27,106 --> 00:02:28,190
THE 13TH SEASON

31
00:02:28,315 --> 00:02:29,149
Are you crazy?

32
00:02:30,025 --> 00:02:31,485
What are you doing?

33
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:33,863
I told you I was quitting.

34
00:02:33,988 --> 00:02:36,532
I've been saying over and over
that I'm quitting!

35
00:02:37,575 --> 00:02:39,118
But why won't anyone listen?

36
00:02:39,243 --> 00:02:41,704
Why won't anyone believe me?

37
00:02:45,541 --> 00:02:48,961
Mom, I said it
because I'm truly struggling.

38
00:02:49,086 --> 00:02:51,380
I felt so bad for you

39
00:02:51,505 --> 00:02:54,508
and ashamed of myself.
But it was just too hard,

40
00:02:54,633 --> 00:02:57,052
so I mustered all my courage to tell you.

41
00:02:58,053 --> 00:02:58,929
So…

42
00:03:00,472 --> 00:03:02,141
you're actually going to quit?

43
00:03:02,266 --> 00:03:05,394
Yeah, I'll quit for real.

44
00:03:05,519 --> 00:03:07,062
I'm never doing film ever again!

45
00:03:07,187 --> 00:03:09,398
You put your entire youth into it!

46
00:03:09,523 --> 00:03:12,484
How can you just throw it away
because it's hard?

47
00:03:12,610 --> 00:03:14,862
You have to fight even harder.

48
00:03:14,987 --> 00:03:17,531
Grit your teeth and push through.

49
00:03:19,116 --> 00:03:21,952
If you give up now,
you'll be a loser for life.

50
00:03:22,077 --> 00:03:23,245
You hear me?

51
00:03:29,543 --> 00:03:30,377
A loser?

52
00:03:30,502 --> 00:03:32,463
Yes, a loser.

53
00:03:33,964 --> 00:03:34,924
I'm sorry.

54
00:03:36,008 --> 00:03:37,551
Your daughter is a loser.

55
00:03:38,844 --> 00:03:41,680
What are you doing, you little…

56
00:03:41,805 --> 00:03:42,806
What are you…

57
00:03:42,932 --> 00:03:44,934
-How dare you say that?
-Ms. Ma, stop!

58
00:03:45,059 --> 00:03:45,893
That hurts.

59
00:03:48,270 --> 00:03:49,563
Calm down.

60
00:03:51,231 --> 00:03:53,984
Calm down and put that down.

61
00:04:18,092 --> 00:04:21,095
I'm sorry I didn't tell you in advance.

62
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:22,554
Obviously, you couldn't.

63
00:04:23,222 --> 00:04:25,599
She probably threatened you.

64
00:04:27,142 --> 00:04:28,936
She gave you a hard time.

65
00:04:30,646 --> 00:04:34,733
Still, out of the four of you,
Lee Mi-do is the kindest.

66
00:04:34,858 --> 00:04:37,361
Lee Yeong-do is the softest.

67
00:04:37,486 --> 00:04:39,822
Lee Wan-do is the meanest.

68
00:04:40,614 --> 00:04:42,199
And as for you…

69
00:04:45,786 --> 00:04:47,121
I'm not going to say.

70
00:04:48,038 --> 00:04:49,707
You always keep quiet.

71
00:04:49,832 --> 00:04:52,292
So I should have a secret too.

72
00:04:55,629 --> 00:04:58,173
Hurry up and go comfort the kind one.

73
00:04:58,298 --> 00:05:01,051
You're better at comforting her than I am.

74
00:05:34,918 --> 00:05:37,212
She must've won about 20 of them.

75
00:05:39,089 --> 00:05:40,340
Thirty-two.

76
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:49,725
Are you really

77
00:05:50,851 --> 00:05:52,352
sure about this?

78
00:05:55,814 --> 00:05:57,483
Are you sure you won't regret it?

79
00:05:58,692 --> 00:06:02,571
I interviewed last week
and had my first day today.

80
00:06:04,615 --> 00:06:05,991
It's decent. Good prospects too.

81
00:06:09,495 --> 00:06:11,371
My life

82
00:06:12,748 --> 00:06:14,416
and my relationship with you…

83
00:06:16,210 --> 00:06:18,170
have both hit rock bottom, anyway.

84
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:25,511
Honestly, I'm terrified,

85
00:06:27,846 --> 00:06:29,556
but I'm also not afraid.

86
00:06:38,148 --> 00:06:39,608
Did you ask her?

87
00:06:44,738 --> 00:06:46,448
Would you date me for just a month?

88
00:06:51,954 --> 00:06:52,788
Yes.

89
00:06:54,915 --> 00:06:55,833
I would.

90
00:06:58,252 --> 00:06:59,545
Let's date.

91
00:07:01,755 --> 00:07:02,589
You and me.

92
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:12,015
What about you?

93
00:07:16,186 --> 00:07:19,314
Just for a month,
do you want to go crazy with me?

94
00:07:20,357 --> 00:07:21,608
Can you handle it?

95
00:07:26,697 --> 00:07:27,823
You know…

96
00:07:32,619 --> 00:07:34,663
If you date me,
you'll never go back to him.

97
00:07:37,583 --> 00:07:40,919
I'll do everything I can to win you over.

98
00:07:53,974 --> 00:07:55,184
Just one month.

99
00:07:58,061 --> 00:07:59,897
We're just breaking up for a month.

100
00:08:00,022 --> 00:08:01,607
-And--
-For that month,

101
00:08:04,151 --> 00:08:06,570
let's do our best with our new partners.

102
00:08:07,362 --> 00:08:09,239
And starting right now…

103
00:08:12,284 --> 00:08:14,620
we are officially on a break.

104
00:08:51,531 --> 00:08:57,412
9. DO YOU REMEMBER WHEN WE FELL IN LOVE?

105
00:09:09,466 --> 00:09:11,677
-Let me ask you something.
-I'll say something first.

106
00:09:14,513 --> 00:09:15,555
You're right.

107
00:09:16,181 --> 00:09:17,349
I have feelings for you.

108
00:09:17,474 --> 00:09:19,726
Based on my objective self-analysis,

109
00:09:19,851 --> 00:09:23,438
I relied on you
during the sweet potato scandal,

110
00:09:23,563 --> 00:09:28,068
and I'm making the error of mistaking
platonic feelings for romance,

111
00:09:28,193 --> 00:09:29,319
I think.

112
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:33,031
My goal is to fix that in a month.

113
00:09:36,243 --> 00:09:37,911
I don't think it's an error.

114
00:09:40,330 --> 00:09:43,292
You like me. Romantically.

115
00:09:44,668 --> 00:09:46,628
Like you said,
you struggled with the scandal,

116
00:09:46,753 --> 00:09:48,672
and I was the only one you had.

117
00:09:48,797 --> 00:09:52,342
But the problem is,
I got transferred because of you.

118
00:09:52,467 --> 00:09:55,012
That must have been the trigger.

119
00:09:55,721 --> 00:09:58,640
When you feel guilty toward someone,

120
00:09:58,765 --> 00:10:01,143
that feeling gains momentum and strength.

121
00:10:01,810 --> 00:10:03,270
You feel sorry, so you care.

122
00:10:03,395 --> 00:10:06,648
You care, so you keep looking at them.
Then you keep thinking of them.

123
00:10:06,773 --> 00:10:07,858
But that someone is me.

124
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:09,735
I'm handsome.

125
00:10:11,445 --> 00:10:12,738
I have a mature charm.

126
00:10:12,863 --> 00:10:14,823
I rock a suit and have swagger.

127
00:10:14,948 --> 00:10:16,658
My intellect makes others feel secure.

128
00:10:16,783 --> 00:10:19,077
Plus, I'm great at my job. It's insane.

129
00:10:20,037 --> 00:10:21,788
Considering all of this,

130
00:10:21,913 --> 00:10:24,958
it's natural for you
to like your senior colleague.

131
00:10:25,083 --> 00:10:27,669
Especially since that senior colleague
is me.

132
00:10:31,590 --> 00:10:33,258
Are you crazy?

133
00:10:34,843 --> 00:10:36,094
So what are you saying?

134
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:39,097
That I'm head over heels for you?

135
00:10:39,222 --> 00:10:41,183
Are you really saying
something so ridiculous?

136
00:10:41,308 --> 00:10:42,517
No.

137
00:10:43,143 --> 00:10:47,230
It's just a cringe phase you go through
at your level with a senior.

138
00:10:48,148 --> 00:10:49,024
That's what I mean.

139
00:10:50,317 --> 00:10:51,693
And in a month,

140
00:10:51,818 --> 00:10:54,112
I'll be a truly embarrassing memory
for you.

141
00:11:01,828 --> 00:11:03,121
What about physical intimacy?

142
00:11:05,749 --> 00:11:08,335
How much touching is allowed?

143
00:11:12,756 --> 00:11:14,007
How much can you tolerate?

144
00:11:16,593 --> 00:11:18,970
We're adults. Why set limits?

145
00:11:19,638 --> 00:11:22,099
Shouldn't everything be allowed?

146
00:11:22,224 --> 00:11:23,642
Is that so?

147
00:11:26,978 --> 00:11:28,063
Shall we go?

148
00:11:51,670 --> 00:11:52,671
Going up.

149
00:11:54,965 --> 00:11:56,133
Doors closing.

150
00:12:17,529 --> 00:12:18,363
Shower first?

151
00:12:21,032 --> 00:12:22,492
Should I go first?

152
00:12:25,078 --> 00:12:25,996
You shower first.

153
00:12:27,247 --> 00:12:28,373
-Okay.
-Wait, no.

154
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,293
I'll shower first.

155
00:12:54,858 --> 00:12:56,151
Hey.

156
00:12:57,486 --> 00:12:58,528
Park Su-a.

157
00:13:00,155 --> 00:13:01,907
I mean, Park Deok-sun.

158
00:13:02,574 --> 00:13:04,576
A guy asks you to a hotel on date one?

159
00:13:04,701 --> 00:13:06,703
You smack him in the head and leave.

160
00:13:06,828 --> 00:13:08,747
Why follow me blindly like that?

161
00:13:09,331 --> 00:13:12,417
I was just seeing how far you'd go,
and you did it.

162
00:13:12,542 --> 00:13:13,376
You're crazy.

163
00:13:14,961 --> 00:13:19,174
Just like your values,
politics, and morals,

164
00:13:19,299 --> 00:13:21,885
knowing each other's sexual tastes
is essential,

165
00:13:22,844 --> 00:13:23,929
I think.

166
00:13:25,055 --> 00:13:28,225
Physical intimacy is the fastest way
to know someone.

167
00:13:28,350 --> 00:13:32,354
Above all, in South Korea,
we have sexual autonomy.

168
00:13:33,146 --> 00:13:33,980
Say that again.

169
00:13:36,483 --> 00:13:38,944
Two consenting adults coming to a hotel--

170
00:13:41,154 --> 00:13:42,239
Say that again.

171
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:46,076
It isn't a legal issue or anything.

172
00:13:47,035 --> 00:13:47,869
Again.

173
00:13:48,578 --> 00:13:51,122
I don't know why I'm being criticized
when it's not--

174
00:13:51,248 --> 00:13:52,290
Say it again.

175
00:13:52,999 --> 00:13:54,960
Honestly, if we try it

176
00:13:55,085 --> 00:13:56,294
and it's not good,

177
00:13:56,419 --> 00:13:58,547
we'll lose feelings fast and… Hey!

178
00:14:19,442 --> 00:14:20,360
You're right.

179
00:14:21,111 --> 00:14:22,779
I like you more than you know.

180
00:14:24,281 --> 00:14:25,448
That's why this crazy…

181
00:14:26,241 --> 00:14:30,078
I mean, I agreed to this ridiculous
one-month relationship, right?

182
00:14:31,246 --> 00:14:33,206
You also said you were curious about me.

183
00:14:33,331 --> 00:14:34,457
Was that a lie?

184
00:14:34,583 --> 00:14:36,251
I'm only curious about you.

185
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:39,879
It won't work
if your feelings are too deep.

186
00:14:58,481 --> 00:15:01,067
Wow, your stamina is really terrible.

187
00:15:01,192 --> 00:15:04,195
You're practically jobless
with no clients.

188
00:15:04,779 --> 00:15:07,324
I work five days a week at my new job.

189
00:15:07,449 --> 00:15:09,909
Even so,
I got all dressed up to be polite.

190
00:15:10,035 --> 00:15:12,537
Why am I walking 5,000 steps
on a first date?

191
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:15,248
Do you know why?

192
00:15:17,876 --> 00:15:19,294
Do your feet hurt a lot?

193
00:15:19,419 --> 00:15:21,379
Jeez, how can you even ask that?

194
00:15:33,892 --> 00:15:34,851
Just one?

195
00:15:34,976 --> 00:15:36,978
I don't like you enough yet
to give you both.

196
00:16:04,005 --> 00:16:05,048
What the…

197
00:16:12,472 --> 00:16:15,141
"I'm the illegitimate son
from one of these homes."

198
00:16:15,266 --> 00:16:16,851
Don't you dare say that crap.

199
00:16:19,979 --> 00:16:22,816
So your lack of imagination
is why you failed as a director.

200
00:16:23,441 --> 00:16:26,986
You got dumped by Seo Ju-hyeok
and have no cases, so shut up.

201
00:16:29,114 --> 00:16:30,990
They found me here.

202
00:16:31,116 --> 00:16:34,035
My so-called mother
watched too many dramas.

203
00:16:34,619 --> 00:16:37,580
She thought I'd grow up rich
if I was left outside a mansion.

204
00:16:41,584 --> 00:16:42,961
I'll show you

205
00:16:44,295 --> 00:16:45,422
where my misery began.

206
00:16:57,809 --> 00:16:59,394
Why did you bring me here?

207
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:02,188
To get your pity.

208
00:17:04,232 --> 00:17:07,235
I figured pity is my best shot
at winning you over.

209
00:17:08,111 --> 00:17:10,780
So I'm planning to give it my all
for one month.

210
00:17:13,241 --> 00:17:14,325
What do you say?

211
00:17:15,243 --> 00:17:17,495
Does looking at me make your heart ache?

212
00:17:20,165 --> 00:17:21,249
What do you think?

213
00:17:23,084 --> 00:17:24,252
Guess it's not enough.

214
00:17:26,337 --> 00:17:27,547
Why aren't you asking

215
00:17:28,339 --> 00:17:31,509
why I suggested we date?

216
00:17:33,720 --> 00:17:34,721
To make you feel guilty.

217
00:17:36,556 --> 00:17:39,517
I only know two ways
to win someone's heart.

218
00:17:39,642 --> 00:17:41,436
Making them feel guilty,

219
00:17:43,396 --> 00:17:44,731
or hurting them.

220
00:17:51,863 --> 00:17:53,740
I can get over you in a month.

221
00:17:57,869 --> 00:18:00,830
My feelings for you
have definitely already peaked.

222
00:18:00,955 --> 00:18:04,542
But this is just my feelings
getting ahead of themselves.

223
00:18:04,667 --> 00:18:07,879
I only do what benefits me,
so I never take a loss.

224
00:18:08,004 --> 00:18:09,923
I'll definitely move on in a month.

225
00:18:10,048 --> 00:18:12,842
I'll reject you
even if you say you like me.

226
00:18:14,511 --> 00:18:15,428
That's a promise.

227
00:18:19,474 --> 00:18:21,810
Answer me. You promised.

228
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:29,609
Then do me one favor.

229
00:18:30,944 --> 00:18:32,028
What is it?

230
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:40,370
After our dates,
let's hold eye contact for ten seconds.

231
00:18:42,247 --> 00:18:44,624
If I last ten seconds, I'm over you.

232
00:18:52,674 --> 00:18:53,758
Let's do it now.

233
00:19:07,897 --> 00:19:09,440
Wow, you like me this much?

234
00:19:11,276 --> 00:19:13,194
Deok-sun, what are you going to do?

235
00:19:21,327 --> 00:19:22,787
Tomorrow, I'll last four seconds.

236
00:19:37,635 --> 00:19:39,888
YEONHWARU

237
00:20:31,064 --> 00:20:33,858
Come on, is this really counseling?

238
00:20:33,983 --> 00:20:35,276
It is.

239
00:20:35,860 --> 00:20:37,111
She says it is.

240
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:40,698
You guys are divorced.
Should you be working together?

241
00:20:40,823 --> 00:20:41,699
We should.

242
00:20:41,824 --> 00:20:42,867
She says we should.

243
00:20:47,372 --> 00:20:50,041
Mom, Dad, let me change my name.

244
00:20:51,084 --> 00:20:53,127
My name is too old-fashioned.

245
00:20:53,252 --> 00:20:54,504
I really hate it.

246
00:20:54,629 --> 00:20:55,463
-No!
-No!

247
00:21:04,931 --> 00:21:08,893
Did he fall into the toilet or what?
Why is he taking so long?

248
00:21:09,894 --> 00:21:12,230
I'll try to talk him out of it.

249
00:21:12,355 --> 00:21:15,108
A name change would make
dealing with banks and stuff a hassle.

250
00:21:18,945 --> 00:21:21,197
Isn't it about time we told him?

251
00:21:22,991 --> 00:21:24,033
About our divorce.

252
00:21:25,785 --> 00:21:27,870
What was the real reason?

253
00:21:33,459 --> 00:21:35,044
Honestly, back then…

254
00:21:36,796 --> 00:21:38,423
I loved you so much,

255
00:21:39,590 --> 00:21:41,551
so I asked for a divorce.

256
00:21:42,301 --> 00:21:44,178
But you didn't stop me.

257
00:21:47,849 --> 00:21:48,975
Hey, Ko Mun-yeong.

258
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:53,312
All I remember
is crying and begging you to stay.

259
00:21:54,230 --> 00:21:55,314
What are you saying?

260
00:21:55,440 --> 00:21:56,774
No.

261
00:21:57,859 --> 00:21:58,860
You let me go.

262
00:21:59,569 --> 00:22:00,611
And back then,

263
00:22:02,030 --> 00:22:03,489
I loved you so much.

264
00:22:12,915 --> 00:22:14,083
I…

265
00:22:14,709 --> 00:22:16,753
I'll just take the bus.

266
00:22:16,878 --> 00:22:18,921
I hope you understand.

267
00:22:21,215 --> 00:22:23,134
Hey, Sang-su. Sang-su!

268
00:22:34,103 --> 00:22:36,773
Dry it completely first.
Moisture will make it short-circuit.

269
00:22:37,523 --> 00:22:39,317
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

270
00:22:43,154 --> 00:22:45,907
Shouldn't we compensate him?

271
00:22:46,032 --> 00:22:48,951
No, he volunteers his expertise.
He used to be a pro.

272
00:22:49,077 --> 00:22:49,911
Really?

273
00:22:57,043 --> 00:22:59,504
Your third chemo is tomorrow.
Where are you going?

274
00:23:00,379 --> 00:23:04,634
It spread to my peritoneum,
and Opdivo isn't working.

275
00:23:05,551 --> 00:23:09,138
No, there's another way. There has to be.

276
00:23:09,263 --> 00:23:12,266
My mom, my dad, and my doctor…

277
00:23:14,227 --> 00:23:15,436
all gave up on me.

278
00:23:18,981 --> 00:23:21,109
Now you just need to give up too.

279
00:23:38,584 --> 00:23:39,627
If you…

280
00:23:40,878 --> 00:23:42,463
just leave like this

281
00:23:42,588 --> 00:23:44,382
and go die,

282
00:23:45,758 --> 00:23:47,135
I'm going to live recklessly.

283
00:23:47,718 --> 00:23:49,137
I'll completely ruin my life.

284
00:23:49,804 --> 00:23:51,514
I'll quit diving,

285
00:23:51,639 --> 00:23:54,016
I'll drink every day,
and I'll live like a wreck.

286
00:23:54,976 --> 00:23:56,644
And I'll…

287
00:23:58,521 --> 00:24:01,232
live a more pathetic life
than my sister's.

288
00:24:02,400 --> 00:24:04,735
I'm not lying. I mean it, so…

289
00:24:05,570 --> 00:24:08,489
if you want to see me ruin my life,

290
00:24:09,448 --> 00:24:10,825
then go ahead and die.

291
00:24:52,241 --> 00:24:53,367
Give it to me.

292
00:24:53,492 --> 00:24:55,786
No, you know I can't sleep without it.

293
00:24:56,954 --> 00:24:57,788
Bo-ra.

294
00:24:59,081 --> 00:25:01,709
From now on,
I'll be right beside you with this

295
00:25:02,460 --> 00:25:04,545
every night until you fall asleep.

296
00:25:05,755 --> 00:25:08,925
But once you're asleep, I'm taking it.

297
00:25:10,551 --> 00:25:12,053
Since you can't sleep without it,

298
00:25:12,637 --> 00:25:16,098
you won't go anywhere without it, right?

299
00:25:20,811 --> 00:25:22,188
I'm sorry, Wan-do.

300
00:25:25,816 --> 00:25:27,318
And thank you

301
00:25:28,194 --> 00:25:29,737
for not giving up on me.

302
00:25:49,882 --> 00:25:51,300
How deep today?

303
00:25:51,425 --> 00:25:53,469
150 meters.

304
00:25:54,595 --> 00:25:55,596
If you ask me,

305
00:25:55,721 --> 00:25:57,306
Bo-ra lied to you.

306
00:25:57,974 --> 00:26:00,393
That music box isn't down there.

307
00:26:02,687 --> 00:26:03,938
Yes, it is.

308
00:26:04,855 --> 00:26:06,232
I just can't find it.

309
00:26:13,739 --> 00:26:14,573
Ho.

310
00:26:16,409 --> 00:26:17,243
What if

311
00:26:18,494 --> 00:26:19,578
Bo-ra…

312
00:26:21,122 --> 00:26:23,624
can't sleep up there either because of me?

313
00:26:27,044 --> 00:26:29,297
It's heaven.
They must have a cure for insomnia.

314
00:26:32,341 --> 00:26:34,260
Hell might not have any, though.

315
00:26:39,724 --> 00:26:40,766
It's been three days.

316
00:26:41,851 --> 00:26:43,269
I'll give you five days max.

317
00:26:44,103 --> 00:26:45,271
But no more than that.

318
00:26:46,605 --> 00:26:48,190
Eat even if you don't want to.

319
00:26:48,316 --> 00:26:51,861
Go to karaoke even if you don't want to.
Force yourself to smile.

320
00:26:52,778 --> 00:26:55,823
I'm not asking you
to humor your worried family.

321
00:26:55,948 --> 00:26:57,658
If you force yourself,

322
00:26:58,659 --> 00:27:00,328
you'll get used to it.

323
00:27:02,371 --> 00:27:04,165
You'll survive somehow.

324
00:27:10,421 --> 00:27:11,630
Is that what you did?

325
00:27:12,673 --> 00:27:13,758
Did that…

326
00:27:16,218 --> 00:27:17,303
make life go on?

327
00:27:24,560 --> 00:27:26,354
Did Sol call you again?

328
00:27:28,814 --> 00:27:30,066
ANON TEMPORARY CHILD SHELTER

329
00:27:30,191 --> 00:27:34,653
Actually, since the new semester started,
I think he's struggling more emotionally.

330
00:27:34,779 --> 00:27:37,114
His mother's arrest
must have been a huge shock,

331
00:27:37,239 --> 00:27:40,076
and he had to transfer schools suddenly.

332
00:27:40,701 --> 00:27:43,079
Is my foster application on hold again?

333
00:27:43,788 --> 00:27:45,915
I've completed my community service,

334
00:27:46,040 --> 00:27:48,584
and finished the foster parent training.

335
00:27:48,709 --> 00:27:50,127
Are there more documents I need?

336
00:27:50,252 --> 00:27:52,713
Well, since you're single

337
00:27:52,838 --> 00:27:55,383
with no extra hands around to help…

338
00:27:57,343 --> 00:28:01,055
It'd be easier
if Sol's brother applied with you.

339
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:03,182
Have you not told him yet?

340
00:28:06,936 --> 00:28:08,521
I contacted Pastor Kim,

341
00:28:08,646 --> 00:28:11,273
and he said he'd return
as soon as possible.

342
00:28:11,399 --> 00:28:14,860
Until then, we have someone
with foster experience, so we--

343
00:28:28,916 --> 00:28:30,334
ANON TEMPORARY CHILD SHELTER

344
00:28:36,924 --> 00:28:39,009
I first saw him three years ago.

345
00:28:39,677 --> 00:28:41,720
After that, he'd call once a month,

346
00:28:41,846 --> 00:28:43,597
and I'd buy him meals.

347
00:28:44,807 --> 00:28:47,476
He was sent to the shelter
after Choi Hwa-young was arrested.

348
00:28:47,601 --> 00:28:49,895
He struggled to adjust,
so he called often.

349
00:28:50,563 --> 00:28:51,981
It's true I didn't tell you.

350
00:28:52,565 --> 00:28:55,234
I tried to handle it on my own,

351
00:28:55,359 --> 00:28:57,945
but I couldn't stop him.
I'm sorry about that.

352
00:28:58,070 --> 00:28:59,947
Do you know why he contacted us?

353
00:29:01,407 --> 00:29:03,075
It's for Choi Hwa-young's petition.

354
00:29:03,200 --> 00:29:05,077
The trial is set for next week.

355
00:29:05,202 --> 00:29:07,830
Namgung, Sol is ten years old.

356
00:29:08,539 --> 00:29:10,916
It's for the petition,
but he missed you too.

357
00:29:11,041 --> 00:29:12,585
He's not an ordinary kid.

358
00:29:14,712 --> 00:29:16,130
I know better than anyone.

359
00:29:17,506 --> 00:29:19,216
I was like that at his age.

360
00:29:24,555 --> 00:29:25,890
I won't say this again.

361
00:29:27,099 --> 00:29:28,225
Stay out of this.

362
00:29:29,518 --> 00:29:30,644
No, I can't.

363
00:29:36,775 --> 00:29:37,902
Hey, Lee Mi-do.

364
00:29:39,028 --> 00:29:40,654
You must have forgotten,

365
00:29:41,697 --> 00:29:42,823
but we broke up.

366
00:29:43,449 --> 00:29:44,950
We aren't together anymore.

367
00:29:45,743 --> 00:29:48,078
Did you forget
you have no right to interfere?

368
00:29:48,871 --> 00:29:50,498
I know, but…

369
00:29:54,001 --> 00:29:56,670
I wasn't just your girlfriend.

370
00:29:59,298 --> 00:30:02,343
You help Lee Yeong-do and Lee Wan-do.
So I'm doing this too.

371
00:30:02,468 --> 00:30:04,178
Are our situations the same?

372
00:30:05,471 --> 00:30:07,890
Do I have to spell it out for you?

373
00:30:10,309 --> 00:30:12,353
I'm telling you clearly.

374
00:30:14,063 --> 00:30:15,648
Don't interfere in this anymore.

375
00:30:15,773 --> 00:30:17,316
I won't hold back next time.

376
00:30:48,430 --> 00:30:49,848
Hello. My name is Sol.

377
00:30:49,974 --> 00:30:52,810
Who's that mini Namgung?

378
00:30:52,935 --> 00:30:54,311
He said he's Sol.

379
00:30:54,436 --> 00:30:57,147
It's Sol,
like in do-re-mi-fa-sol-la-ti-do.

380
00:30:57,273 --> 00:30:58,440
I'm Han Sol.

381
00:31:00,901 --> 00:31:05,197
"All I remember
is crying and begging you to stay."

382
00:31:07,783 --> 00:31:08,826
Yes!

383
00:31:09,577 --> 00:31:12,288
The pastor taking him in
had an emergency.

384
00:31:12,913 --> 00:31:15,040
He'll stay with us for a few days.

385
00:31:15,624 --> 00:31:18,043
Let's get along well, sweetie.

386
00:31:18,168 --> 00:31:19,128
Okay.

387
00:31:22,047 --> 00:31:22,965
Auntie Mi-do!

388
00:31:32,141 --> 00:31:35,853
Auntie Mi-do, you told me to call you
if I was having a hard time.

389
00:31:35,978 --> 00:31:37,855
It was really hard there.

390
00:31:41,442 --> 00:31:45,779
And I finished the book
you bought me last time, Mi-do.

391
00:31:49,783 --> 00:31:52,036
Pretty Mi-do.

392
00:31:53,203 --> 00:31:56,290
Is Assistant Manager Namgung Ho
really mad?

393
00:31:59,585 --> 00:32:01,837
Don't call him that. He's your brother.

394
00:32:01,962 --> 00:32:03,881
I'll talk to him about the petition.

395
00:32:04,006 --> 00:32:04,965
Don't expect much.

396
00:32:05,090 --> 00:32:07,092
You're prettier than Jang Won-young.

397
00:32:07,760 --> 00:32:08,677
Still no.

398
00:32:09,720 --> 00:32:11,347
You saw your brother's face.

399
00:32:11,472 --> 00:32:13,682
Your brother is scary when he's mad.

400
00:32:13,807 --> 00:32:16,894
Is that why he sent my mom to prison?

401
00:32:17,019 --> 00:32:18,437
Because he's mad?

402
00:32:38,832 --> 00:32:40,084
Han Sol.

403
00:32:41,585 --> 00:32:44,505
You think you're the person
who loves your mom the most, right?

404
00:32:46,215 --> 00:32:47,257
But you're wrong.

405
00:32:47,800 --> 00:32:51,053
You've only known your mom for ten years.

406
00:32:51,887 --> 00:32:54,264
But your brother
has known her for 36 years.

407
00:32:56,350 --> 00:32:59,561
Your mom did something wrong,

408
00:32:59,687 --> 00:33:02,064
so she went to prison to be punished.

409
00:33:02,189 --> 00:33:03,232
It wasn't his fault.

410
00:33:10,739 --> 00:33:11,615
Sol.

411
00:33:13,659 --> 00:33:15,786
No matter what anyone else thinks,

412
00:33:17,329 --> 00:33:19,873
you must never hate your brother.

413
00:33:25,796 --> 00:33:28,215
Promise the girl
prettier than Jang Won-young.

414
00:33:29,550 --> 00:33:30,384
Okay?

415
00:33:33,971 --> 00:33:35,055
You won't?

416
00:33:38,559 --> 00:33:39,643
Good boy.

417
00:33:40,894 --> 00:33:42,104
Jeez.

418
00:33:45,774 --> 00:33:47,484
You should go to sleep.

419
00:34:00,164 --> 00:34:03,959
REQUESTING A DRIVER
UP TO THREE MINUTES AWAY

420
00:34:04,084 --> 00:34:06,170
Did everyone go crazy this Friday night?

421
00:34:06,295 --> 00:34:08,380
This is Seoul. Why no taxis?

422
00:34:08,505 --> 00:34:11,842
It's right around the corner.
Why would they come?

423
00:34:12,718 --> 00:34:15,846
You should go back. Sol is at home.

424
00:34:16,889 --> 00:34:19,141
I just came out for some fresh air.

425
00:34:26,857 --> 00:34:27,858
What?

426
00:34:27,983 --> 00:34:29,193
Why are you laughing?

427
00:34:29,818 --> 00:34:32,946
Isn't it funny? You being called Auntie.

428
00:34:34,448 --> 00:34:36,033
He's doing it on purpose.

429
00:34:36,158 --> 00:34:38,327
He knows I hate being called that.

430
00:34:38,452 --> 00:34:39,995
What are you talking about?

431
00:34:40,871 --> 00:34:43,665
You're old enough to be called Auntie now.

432
00:34:43,791 --> 00:34:45,417
Actually,

433
00:34:46,502 --> 00:34:48,545
you are an auntie. A total auntie.

434
00:34:48,670 --> 00:34:49,505
Oh, Mom!

435
00:34:49,630 --> 00:34:52,716
What are you even saying…

436
00:34:55,969 --> 00:34:57,638
He looks a lot like Hoya.

437
00:35:01,558 --> 00:35:02,810
Not even a little.

438
00:35:02,935 --> 00:35:04,311
Come to think of it,

439
00:35:05,062 --> 00:35:07,189
when I first met Hoya,

440
00:35:07,314 --> 00:35:08,774
I was exactly your age.

441
00:35:15,405 --> 00:35:16,281
Your socks.

442
00:35:16,949 --> 00:35:17,783
What?

443
00:35:18,367 --> 00:35:19,660
Goodness.

444
00:35:20,619 --> 00:35:21,578
Jeez.

445
00:35:24,957 --> 00:35:28,836
Do you know why you always
catch a cold around this time?

446
00:35:28,961 --> 00:35:31,004
Because you're so careless.

447
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:33,090
Stop. What are you doing?

448
00:35:33,215 --> 00:35:37,761
Oh, stay still.
The bus won't be here for a while.

449
00:35:37,886 --> 00:35:39,638
Mom, you wear it.

450
00:35:39,763 --> 00:35:42,099
You struggle with asthma
this time of year.

451
00:35:43,225 --> 00:35:44,101
Jeez.

452
00:35:56,530 --> 00:35:58,240
It's your fault.

453
00:35:59,950 --> 00:36:02,786
When you were little,
if you were even slightly hurt,

454
00:36:02,911 --> 00:36:05,873
you'd run to me and say,
"Mom, it hurts."

455
00:36:05,998 --> 00:36:09,042
You'd act like you were dying
and beg for a doctor.

456
00:36:09,751 --> 00:36:12,671
Now that you're all grown up,
you never tell me.

457
00:36:12,796 --> 00:36:13,881
Do you?

458
00:36:14,923 --> 00:36:16,174
So how would I know?

459
00:36:17,843 --> 00:36:19,970
I thought you were dressed warmly.

460
00:36:20,971 --> 00:36:24,224
I never thought the cold wind
would get in through there.

461
00:36:34,109 --> 00:36:37,529
If you act like this,
what does that make me?

462
00:36:38,196 --> 00:36:41,825
I was going to be the one
to apologize first.

463
00:36:43,452 --> 00:36:45,954
I never apologized to you.

464
00:36:46,079 --> 00:36:47,956
I only blamed you.

465
00:36:49,499 --> 00:36:51,627
Then I won't apologize either.

466
00:36:51,752 --> 00:36:53,211
I won't. I don't want to.

467
00:36:54,588 --> 00:36:58,091
I'm so embarrassed.
I feel like I'm going to die.

468
00:37:00,427 --> 00:37:03,889
I get treated like total dirt
every single day.

469
00:37:04,014 --> 00:37:06,433
Those Gen Zers
treat me like absolute garbage.

470
00:37:08,143 --> 00:37:10,354
I'm so humiliated, I could die.

471
00:37:10,479 --> 00:37:13,190
So why are you being like this?

472
00:37:13,315 --> 00:37:16,193
And so… that's why…

473
00:37:16,318 --> 00:37:18,362
Go ahead. Let it all out.

474
00:37:19,112 --> 00:37:22,115
You have to blame your mom
to survive out there.

475
00:37:23,659 --> 00:37:24,785
Oh my.

476
00:37:25,535 --> 00:37:28,038
Who would call you Auntie?

477
00:37:28,163 --> 00:37:29,957
You're still just a baby.

478
00:37:30,624 --> 00:37:34,169
You're the one…
I'm only crying because of you.

479
00:37:51,061 --> 00:37:52,229
Thank you.

480
00:37:56,233 --> 00:37:57,067
Son.

481
00:38:00,529 --> 00:38:03,699
We don't have much time,
so I'll get to the point.

482
00:38:05,158 --> 00:38:06,910
You're here about Sol's custody, right?

483
00:38:09,788 --> 00:38:11,832
Commissary money won't cut it.

484
00:38:11,957 --> 00:38:14,626
A few petitions for leniency?
Obviously not enough.

485
00:38:15,877 --> 00:38:18,839
I want you to hire
the best lawyer you can

486
00:38:18,964 --> 00:38:20,632
to get me out of here.

487
00:38:23,010 --> 00:38:26,013
For the record,
Mi-do came to see me several times.

488
00:38:26,555 --> 00:38:29,725
If you refuse, I'm going to tell Mi-do.

489
00:38:34,021 --> 00:38:35,313
Fine. Understood.

490
00:38:38,275 --> 00:38:40,819
What? Just like that?

491
00:38:40,944 --> 00:38:44,281
But I'm going to ask you
four questions right now.

492
00:38:46,616 --> 00:38:48,869
If you get even one of them right,

493
00:38:49,953 --> 00:38:51,329
I'll accept all your terms.

494
00:38:56,001 --> 00:39:00,172
First, what's Sol's shoe size?

495
00:39:08,472 --> 00:39:11,516
1… 180 millimeters. No, 170.

496
00:39:12,517 --> 00:39:14,144
Kids grow fast these days.

497
00:39:14,269 --> 00:39:18,065
Second, the name of Sol's school.

498
00:39:20,150 --> 00:39:22,152
He's transferred so many times…

499
00:39:23,779 --> 00:39:25,655
I know his old one for sure--

500
00:39:25,781 --> 00:39:30,118
Third, Sol's best friend.

501
00:39:32,287 --> 00:39:33,371
Fourth.

502
00:39:34,331 --> 00:39:35,373
Sol's birthday.

503
00:39:43,757 --> 00:39:45,634
I thought you'd get at least one right.

504
00:39:48,261 --> 00:39:49,679
I'm disappointed, Mom.

505
00:39:52,599 --> 00:39:55,560
You'll get a document
about parental rights today.

506
00:40:12,619 --> 00:40:13,495
Darn it.

507
00:40:14,496 --> 00:40:16,331
HAN TAE-SEUNG LAW OFFICE

508
00:40:22,504 --> 00:40:23,672
Meet my team.

509
00:40:26,466 --> 00:40:30,428
This is Han Tae-seung,
the lawyer working with us starting today.

510
00:40:31,596 --> 00:40:33,557
He's seriously good-looking, right?

511
00:40:33,682 --> 00:40:36,017
We'll hit 100K subs in no time.

512
00:40:42,774 --> 00:40:43,733
Oh, are you…

513
00:40:44,401 --> 00:40:45,485
Director Lee Mi-do?

514
00:40:47,362 --> 00:40:48,238
You are, right?

515
00:40:48,947 --> 00:40:52,617
She directed the movie  The 13th Season.

516
00:40:53,243 --> 00:40:56,037
Wow, I was a huge fan of that movie.

517
00:40:56,163 --> 00:40:57,372
This is awesome.

518
00:40:57,998 --> 00:40:59,666
Should we start with the lighting?

519
00:41:00,500 --> 00:41:02,836
Oh, sure. Let's get ready, then.

520
00:41:02,961 --> 00:41:04,462
Let's do this today! Let's go!

521
00:41:06,214 --> 00:41:07,048
Good luck.

522
00:41:11,970 --> 00:41:12,804
Ms. Lee.

523
00:41:12,929 --> 00:41:13,972
Yes?

524
00:41:14,097 --> 00:41:15,849
You can't plug it in like this.

525
00:41:16,683 --> 00:41:17,559
I'm sorry.

526
00:41:18,768 --> 00:41:20,687
Move it to the right a bit.

527
00:41:20,812 --> 00:41:22,063
No, to the left.

528
00:41:22,189 --> 00:41:23,231
A little more.

529
00:41:23,356 --> 00:41:24,357
Down, down a bit.

530
00:41:24,482 --> 00:41:26,735
You really have no clue, do you?

531
00:41:26,860 --> 00:41:28,361
I'm sorry.

532
00:41:28,486 --> 00:41:30,947
I told you to leave enough headroom.

533
00:41:31,072 --> 00:41:32,908
Yes, I'm sorry.

534
00:41:33,033 --> 00:41:34,117
Gosh, damn it.

535
00:41:34,242 --> 00:41:36,077
-Ms. Lee.
-Yes.

536
00:41:36,203 --> 00:41:37,454
-Ms. Lee.
-Yes.

537
00:41:37,579 --> 00:41:39,456
-Ms. Lee!
-Yes!

538
00:41:54,095 --> 00:41:55,847
I'm telling you this as a friend.

539
00:41:57,432 --> 00:42:00,560
Your style only worked
because they were films.

540
00:42:00,685 --> 00:42:02,395
Editing isn't easy.

541
00:42:02,520 --> 00:42:04,189
TIN CAN BASTARD

542
00:42:07,442 --> 00:42:08,818
Do a movie adaptation.

543
00:42:08,944 --> 00:42:13,073
So, there's this long-term couple,
and the girl cheats.

544
00:42:13,198 --> 00:42:16,076
It starts with the boyfriend
trying to kill her.

545
00:42:22,874 --> 00:42:23,833
And?

546
00:42:23,959 --> 00:42:24,793
Does he?

547
00:42:24,918 --> 00:42:28,171
But here's the fun part.
You know the guy who hit on her?

548
00:42:28,296 --> 00:42:30,757
Turns out, he's also trying to kill her.

549
00:42:31,800 --> 00:42:33,051
Why?

550
00:42:33,176 --> 00:42:36,221
Because actually, her boyfriend
and the guy she cheated with

551
00:42:36,346 --> 00:42:38,598
were the real couple.

552
00:42:39,474 --> 00:42:43,019
So the one who ends up killing her
isn't the boyfriend, but…

553
00:42:44,729 --> 00:42:46,064
Oh, Attorney Han!

554
00:42:46,189 --> 00:42:47,607
Over here.

555
00:42:52,112 --> 00:42:53,154
Director Lee.

556
00:42:54,155 --> 00:42:55,448
It's been a while.

557
00:42:59,411 --> 00:43:00,412
Yes.

558
00:43:01,121 --> 00:43:02,330
Doing good these days?

559
00:43:03,373 --> 00:43:04,499
Have a seat here.

560
00:43:09,504 --> 00:43:11,548
I think he's interested in me.

561
00:43:11,673 --> 00:43:14,968
He kept asking where I was,
so I had no choice.

562
00:43:15,719 --> 00:43:17,387
Take the hint and leave early.

563
00:43:23,727 --> 00:43:25,770
Sir, please take her home safely.

564
00:43:32,527 --> 00:43:34,946
You didn't answer my calls, so I had to.

565
00:43:35,071 --> 00:43:38,783
For someone who had no choice,
you sure had fun with Yeon-ju.

566
00:43:41,786 --> 00:43:42,746
Are you jealous?

567
00:43:47,250 --> 00:43:48,626
Are you going to kill me?

568
00:43:48,752 --> 00:43:50,378
Where's that coming from?

569
00:43:53,840 --> 00:43:56,092
I'm sorry for not answering your calls.

570
00:43:57,761 --> 00:43:59,637
I'm 36 years old,

571
00:43:59,763 --> 00:44:02,390
getting talked down to
by kids half my age,

572
00:44:02,515 --> 00:44:04,225
and scraping by like this.

573
00:44:05,310 --> 00:44:06,144
I hated it.

574
00:44:07,479 --> 00:44:08,688
I felt so pathetic.

575
00:44:09,647 --> 00:44:12,359
I just couldn't bring myself
to answer your calls.

576
00:44:17,447 --> 00:44:19,991
I told you to get back up
if you feel embarrassed.

577
00:44:20,116 --> 00:44:20,950
Funny, right?

578
00:44:23,203 --> 00:44:24,037
Yes.

579
00:44:29,292 --> 00:44:30,794
Serves you right.

580
00:44:31,419 --> 00:44:32,462
Jeez.

581
00:44:36,591 --> 00:44:38,009
I'll buy you a nice meal.

582
00:44:38,760 --> 00:44:40,887
You should eat well at times like this.

583
00:44:48,937 --> 00:44:50,438
I thought it was cute.

584
00:44:51,523 --> 00:44:53,900
A woman who looks
like she's in her twenties,

585
00:44:54,025 --> 00:44:56,361
scraping by and trying so hard to survive.

586
00:44:57,529 --> 00:44:58,863
I thought it was cute.

587
00:45:13,253 --> 00:45:15,046
That wasn't my first time in a hotel.

588
00:45:16,798 --> 00:45:19,843
I just panicked.
I've gone to hotels with a lot of guys.

589
00:45:20,593 --> 00:45:21,845
Really?

590
00:45:22,762 --> 00:45:23,638
How many?

591
00:45:26,516 --> 00:45:29,102
Like, five or six?

592
00:45:32,689 --> 00:45:36,234
No, wait, Sun-cheol's mom called
halfway through, so he left.

593
00:45:37,277 --> 00:45:39,154
Maybe… two?

594
00:45:39,279 --> 00:45:40,572
Come on.

595
00:45:41,322 --> 00:45:42,699
What about you?

596
00:45:42,824 --> 00:45:44,492
How many have you been with?

597
00:45:46,119 --> 00:45:48,371
You're the only one, honey.

598
00:45:49,038 --> 00:45:50,915
Honey, you're my first love.

599
00:45:52,375 --> 00:45:54,961
Honey, that's what you say
when your boyfriend asks.

600
00:45:55,086 --> 00:45:56,546
Don't just say two or three.

601
00:45:58,047 --> 00:45:59,048
Silly.

602
00:46:04,971 --> 00:46:05,930
Let's make eye contact.

603
00:46:06,055 --> 00:46:07,432
We haven't done it today.

604
00:46:07,557 --> 00:46:09,184
You can't even last four seconds.

605
00:46:09,309 --> 00:46:10,185
Still.

606
00:46:10,935 --> 00:46:12,145
We promised.

607
00:46:19,235 --> 00:46:20,195
Whenever you're ready.

608
00:46:23,781 --> 00:46:24,699
I'm ready.

609
00:46:35,793 --> 00:46:38,463
Jeez, do we have to keep doing this?

610
00:46:39,631 --> 00:46:40,924
It's too much pressure.

611
00:46:41,049 --> 00:46:42,634
Not even four seconds?

612
00:46:44,511 --> 00:46:45,845
Should I stop shaving?

613
00:46:46,513 --> 00:46:47,680
What should I do?

614
00:46:49,307 --> 00:46:50,642
Let's try once more.

615
00:46:51,309 --> 00:46:52,894
Something got in my eye.

616
00:46:53,019 --> 00:46:53,895
We're done.

617
00:46:54,020 --> 00:46:56,022
Come on, just one last time.

618
00:47:28,096 --> 00:47:29,806
Since fate brought us here,

619
00:47:30,723 --> 00:47:32,976
how about we discuss some rules

620
00:47:33,851 --> 00:47:34,894
for the next month?

621
00:47:37,564 --> 00:47:41,109
Like dividing up our regular spots
so we don't overlap.

622
00:47:41,693 --> 00:47:42,527
Oh.

623
00:47:43,361 --> 00:47:45,363
Did you two block each other's numbers?

624
00:47:45,822 --> 00:47:47,240
Don't tell me you didn't.

625
00:47:49,200 --> 00:47:50,618
Wow.

626
00:47:51,369 --> 00:47:53,871
Even if it's for a month,
that's basic etiquette.

627
00:47:54,622 --> 00:47:55,623
Don't you agree?

628
00:47:57,250 --> 00:47:59,419
I want one of you to move out.

629
00:47:59,544 --> 00:48:02,547
I don't care who it is.

630
00:48:02,672 --> 00:48:04,257
Living right across each other?

631
00:48:05,133 --> 00:48:06,134
It's not acceptable.

632
00:48:07,427 --> 00:48:08,344
Right?

633
00:48:10,305 --> 00:48:11,723
Shall we get going?

634
00:48:12,557 --> 00:48:13,391
Why?

635
00:48:14,475 --> 00:48:16,019
Our food isn't even out yet.

636
00:48:33,161 --> 00:48:34,203
Unbelievable.

637
00:48:34,329 --> 00:48:36,539
MI-DO - NAMGUNG

638
00:48:52,096 --> 00:48:53,389
I'll be taking this.

639
00:48:53,514 --> 00:48:55,058
Level three.

640
00:48:56,309 --> 00:48:58,269
Lee Mi-do's rage meter is at level three.

641
00:49:03,274 --> 00:49:04,651
Level four.

642
00:49:06,694 --> 00:49:07,904
Want to see level five?

643
00:49:11,949 --> 00:49:14,452
Keep your boyfriend
from acting cocky with me.

644
00:49:17,789 --> 00:49:18,665
Let's go.

645
00:49:20,875 --> 00:49:23,795
Hey, whose fault do you think this is?

646
00:49:38,810 --> 00:49:39,936
It's your fault.

647
00:49:41,562 --> 00:49:43,815
Yours, for being so damn clueless.

648
00:49:46,359 --> 00:49:48,486
Given their history,
you should show some manners.

649
00:50:00,832 --> 00:50:02,875
Let's go, Assistant Manager Namgung.

650
00:50:33,239 --> 00:50:35,867
Ugh, I should have called you "babe."

651
00:50:35,992 --> 00:50:38,077
"Assistant Manager Namgung"? Really?

652
00:50:39,203 --> 00:50:40,830
Is that really the issue here?

653
00:50:41,914 --> 00:50:42,790
What?

654
00:50:42,915 --> 00:50:47,420
Is that woman… I mean, Ms. Lee Mi-do…

655
00:50:48,546 --> 00:50:50,047
getting in your head?

656
00:50:51,716 --> 00:50:52,800
You are.

657
00:50:54,343 --> 00:50:56,512
Your face is so red right now.

658
00:50:56,637 --> 00:50:57,972
You can let go, you know.

659
00:51:02,852 --> 00:51:04,437
Just talk about anything.

660
00:51:05,438 --> 00:51:07,523
Work. Let's talk about work.

661
00:51:11,652 --> 00:51:13,821
How did TF Team 3's cost adjustment go?

662
00:51:13,946 --> 00:51:15,364
Don't even get me started.

663
00:51:15,490 --> 00:51:17,825
I worked late all week because of that.

664
00:51:18,910 --> 00:51:22,205
But Manager Eom pulled it off.

665
00:51:23,498 --> 00:51:24,332
How?

666
00:51:25,708 --> 00:51:30,171
Imported raw material prices vary
based on local supply, right?

667
00:51:30,296 --> 00:51:33,508
He pulled off a bit of a bluff
using the increased crop volume.

668
00:51:34,884 --> 00:51:36,010
That's a relief.

669
00:51:36,135 --> 00:51:39,847
If it didn't pass, our second-half launch
would've been tough.

670
00:51:43,768 --> 00:51:46,437
I think I've finally calmed down.

671
00:52:05,873 --> 00:52:07,375
Whenever someone asks me…

672
00:52:09,919 --> 00:52:12,630
what my happiest memory is,

673
00:52:14,090 --> 00:52:17,677
I say it's seeing Lake Lucerne at 22.

674
00:52:19,804 --> 00:52:23,182
It was so beautiful. I was speechless,
just staring at it for a moment.

675
00:52:26,519 --> 00:52:28,396
But that's a lie.

676
00:52:31,524 --> 00:52:33,276
What actually comes to mind

677
00:52:34,735 --> 00:52:37,655
is incredibly ordinary
and unsophisticated.

678
00:52:42,952 --> 00:52:45,288
The day my dad came back
from training camp,

679
00:52:46,998 --> 00:52:49,333
I stood by the road closest to our house,

680
00:52:49,917 --> 00:52:50,960
waiting for him.

681
00:52:53,629 --> 00:52:55,673
His team bus arrived,

682
00:52:56,591 --> 00:52:58,009
he got off,

683
00:52:58,801 --> 00:53:00,887
and he carried me home on his back.

684
00:53:05,391 --> 00:53:08,352
Strangely, that's my happiest memory.

685
00:53:10,396 --> 00:53:12,690
Do you know what's my goal for the month?

686
00:53:14,984 --> 00:53:16,903
If someone asks you

687
00:53:17,820 --> 00:53:20,197
what your happiest memory is,

688
00:53:21,073 --> 00:53:24,076
you'll probably think of Ms. Lee.

689
00:53:24,577 --> 00:53:26,245
But in that moment,

690
00:53:27,663 --> 00:53:28,664
for just a second,

691
00:53:31,292 --> 00:53:33,878
I want a memory of us to cross your mind.

692
00:53:35,755 --> 00:53:36,797
And I will

693
00:53:37,632 --> 00:53:38,466
make sure

694
00:53:40,092 --> 00:53:41,260
that happens.

695
00:53:53,022 --> 00:53:54,607
It started back in Haemado.

696
00:53:56,901 --> 00:53:59,028
I've liked you since Haemado.

697
00:54:03,199 --> 00:54:04,825
You're my first love.

698
00:54:16,545 --> 00:54:18,005
I did nothing wrong.

699
00:54:19,215 --> 00:54:20,883
Anyone would've done the same.

700
00:54:28,015 --> 00:54:30,559
When I asked you to date me for a month,

701
00:54:31,227 --> 00:54:32,478
I was just using you.

702
00:54:34,689 --> 00:54:37,024
I had to date you

703
00:54:37,149 --> 00:54:39,026
so Namgung would see other women.

704
00:54:41,737 --> 00:54:44,490
I hurt him so much.

705
00:54:45,574 --> 00:54:47,910
I thought me getting hurt
would make things even.

706
00:54:54,667 --> 00:54:56,377
I know why you like me.

707
00:54:58,129 --> 00:54:59,630
Namgung and I,

708
00:55:01,257 --> 00:55:02,675
we look special, don't we?

709
00:55:04,093 --> 00:55:06,220
And that's what you want, right?

710
00:55:07,805 --> 00:55:08,723
You're right.

711
00:55:10,683 --> 00:55:12,393
I want it.

712
00:55:14,854 --> 00:55:18,190
I want everything you give Namgung Ho.

713
00:55:18,941 --> 00:55:20,234
All of it.

714
00:55:35,499 --> 00:55:36,709
Let me ask you something.

715
00:55:39,920 --> 00:55:44,341
Before, you said if you had to save
either Namgung Ho or me,

716
00:55:44,467 --> 00:55:47,553
you'd save him
without a second thought, right?

717
00:55:49,055 --> 00:55:49,972
What if…

718
00:55:52,308 --> 00:55:54,518
it was your father instead of me?

719
00:55:57,688 --> 00:55:59,273
If it were your father,

720
00:56:02,651 --> 00:56:04,904
would you still save Namgung Ho?

721
00:56:26,383 --> 00:56:28,010
It started back in Haemado.

722
00:56:29,386 --> 00:56:31,472
I've liked you since Haemado.

723
00:56:32,139 --> 00:56:34,183
You're my first love.

724
00:56:41,482 --> 00:56:43,943
YEONHUI-DONG TWIN FISTS

725
00:56:44,068 --> 00:56:45,861
He's such a gentle kid.

726
00:56:45,986 --> 00:56:47,780
He's gentler than you, Hoya.

727
00:56:49,907 --> 00:56:52,159
DELETE

728
00:57:07,716 --> 00:57:11,137
I thought you'd get at least one right.
I'm disappointed, Mom.

729
00:57:12,304 --> 00:57:13,931
Are you really doing this?

730
00:57:14,056 --> 00:57:15,266
Ho.

731
00:57:29,071 --> 00:57:30,281
Son.

732
00:57:41,167 --> 00:57:44,378
On May 12, 2025…

733
00:57:47,256 --> 00:57:48,424
on Sol's birthday,

734
00:57:49,592 --> 00:57:52,928
he took 10,000 won from your wallet.

735
00:57:53,053 --> 00:57:56,182
And in front of his best friend,
Eom Ji-eun,

736
00:57:58,100 --> 00:58:01,395
you struck him in the face
with a shoe three times.

737
00:58:06,734 --> 00:58:09,278
Shop owners near Daejun Elementary
reported it,

738
00:58:09,403 --> 00:58:11,030
and child abuse charges were filed.

739
00:58:11,155 --> 00:58:14,241
But it ended with a brief statement
calling it discipline.

740
00:58:15,618 --> 00:58:18,329
You were released without any punishment.

741
00:58:20,998 --> 00:58:23,417
That happened nine times
in Han Sol's life.

742
00:58:25,628 --> 00:58:27,755
And 12 times in mine.

743
00:58:29,673 --> 00:58:31,342
Do you know what I felt…

744
00:58:33,761 --> 00:58:35,429
the first time I met…

745
00:58:37,223 --> 00:58:39,683
the people I love and am grateful to…

746
00:58:41,143 --> 00:58:43,562
thanks to you?

747
00:58:47,149 --> 00:58:48,651
Resentment.

748
00:58:49,985 --> 00:58:51,654
Resentment that I survived.

749
00:58:51,779 --> 00:58:52,988
Do you know that?

750
00:59:28,524 --> 00:59:29,566
What if…

751
00:59:30,567 --> 00:59:35,072
If it were your father,
would you still save Namgung Ho?

752
00:59:38,575 --> 00:59:42,162
How can you love the man
who caused your father's death?

753
01:00:27,124 --> 01:00:30,502
Namgung and I first met 29 years ago.

754
01:00:32,463 --> 01:00:35,799
It was an unusually cold winter
on the Gangneung coast.

755
01:01:00,699 --> 01:01:02,659
Oh my God. Honey, wake up.

756
01:01:04,036 --> 01:01:05,162
Wake up.

757
01:01:05,287 --> 01:01:06,288
Please wake up!

758
01:01:06,413 --> 01:01:08,040
I said wake up!

759
01:01:17,299 --> 01:01:22,137
The day I met Namgung
was the saddest day of my life.

760
01:01:23,263 --> 01:01:24,932
Wake up!

761
01:01:26,475 --> 01:01:31,271
And that day was the day
Namgung died for the twelfth time.

762
01:01:32,356 --> 01:01:33,357
Honey!

763
01:02:39,631 --> 01:02:42,676
TAKE GOOD CARE OF HER
UNTIL SHE CAN AFFORD TO BUY AN APARTMENT

764
01:02:42,843 --> 01:02:44,511
LEE MI-DO

765
01:02:47,639 --> 01:02:49,266
THANK YOU TO KIM YOON-HYE
FOR HER SPECIAL APPEARANCE

766
01:02:50,184 --> 01:02:51,727
Huh? He's your junior from the army.

767
01:02:51,852 --> 01:02:53,937
Trying to fill the void
of the father you killed?

768
01:02:54,062 --> 01:02:56,690
So, it was you who made Mi-do disappear.

769
01:02:56,815 --> 01:03:00,235
Namgung. I just wanted
to give you everything.

770
01:03:00,360 --> 01:03:05,282
Can you tell me what you said
at the convenience store one more time?

771
01:03:05,407 --> 01:03:06,283
Ho!

772
01:03:06,408 --> 01:03:07,784
I won't hate you.

773
01:03:07,910 --> 01:03:09,620
I can't leave Namgung.

774
01:03:09,745 --> 01:03:11,788
I have to be there for Namgung.

775
01:03:13,499 --> 01:03:15,459
Subtitle translation by Soya Back
